	(text "A single 8MHz resonator requiring no additional\n parts, placed as close as possible to the pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 195.58 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "03bb8f74-29d8-4220-a26a-59eda667da1c")
	)
	(text "ADC18\nADC19"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 191.262 90.424 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "05371d0b-d78e-4ae8-b6e4-bb25f5361849")
	)
	(text "A single capacitor to ground combined with the\ninternal pull up forms an RC which charges and\nensures a short (~3ms) reset pulse on power applied."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 70.104 38.862 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "1b7fba71-e8cc-4c4e-bed6-cd4c369e481c")
	)
	(text "This weak pulldown ensures\nboot=0 (normal boot) whilst \nallowing the SWD port \nto still operate."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 69.85 137.922 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify right)
		)
		(uuid "25c0f909-1f5f-4633-8799-c3badceeb5c8")
	)
	(text "These are all the decoupling the datasheet\ncalls for."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175.768 48.006 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2cfd2d3b-e119-4236-a8fa-8053f23e713b")
	)
	(text "Chosen this G0 series micro as it has\n36KB RAM and 128KBytes Flash which should be\nmore than enough than actually required. It is\nessentially where the small 32pin package and\nthe minimal ram/flash meet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.058 70.104 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7efd4f54-2d80-4d0c-b02c-877ae4c335ee")
	)
	(text "Renamed to \"In Position\" from \"Brake\" as \nit is actually a digital output indicating now is\nthe right time to apply the brake. A simple implementation\nmight drive a relay coil from this but we're more likely\nto CPU control a brake more intelligently with PWM."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 258.064 108.204 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify right)
		)
		(uuid "d0349d01-3eba-4861-9c62-cfcb98294159")
	)
